# Local request examples. Tokens below are FAKE placeholders, never real secrets.
# Send requests individually after replacing placeholders. Nothing in this file
# runs automatically. Sandbox actions mutate only the local app unless explicitly
# labeled as a provider call / outbound webhook registration.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4317
@brandId = brand_bloom
@bagId = REPLACE_WITH_OWN_BAG_ID
@importId = REPLACE_WITH_IMPORT_ID
@webhookEndpointId = REPLACE_WITH_ENDPOINT_ID
@eventId = REPLACE_WITH_OWN_EVENT_ID
@apiKey = avf_test_REPLACE_WITH_KEY_FROM_OWNER_WORKSPACE
@clientId = REPLACE_WITH_AVAFEM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID
@clientSecret = REPLACE_WITH_AVAFEM_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET
@accessToken = REPLACE_WITH_ONE_HOUR_AVAFEM_ACCESS_TOKEN
@sessionCookie = avf_session=REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_OWNER_COOKIE
@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_OWNER_CSRF_TOKEN

### Health; no authentication required
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Local browser bootstrap: copy csrfToken and Set-Cookie for OWNER examples.
# Only available on the loopback development listener. Do not expose publicly.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/session

### OWNER: create a scoped static brand API key (shown once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/brands/{{brandId}}/credentials
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "api_key",
  "label": "Local integration example",
  "scopes": ["catalog:read", "catalog:write", "orders:read", "orders:fulfill", "payouts:read", "refunds:write"]
}

### OWNER: create an Avafem OAuth client (not a Shopify OAuth client)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/brands/{{brandId}}/credentials
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "oauth_client",
  "label": "Local OAuth example",
  "scopes": ["orders:read", "orders:fulfill", "payouts:read", "refunds:write"]
}

### Exchange Avafem client credentials for a one-hour bearer token
# Replace placeholders; requested scopes must be a subset of the client grant.
POST {{baseUrl}}/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}&scope=orders%3Aread%20orders%3Afulfill%20payouts%3Aread%20refunds%3Awrite

### Read own Bags with a static API key
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/bags?status=awaiting_shipment
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Read one own Bag with an OAuth access token
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/bags/{{bagId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Create a SYNTHETIC order for the credential's own brand
# No card is charged. Reusing the same key/body replays for 24h.
# Change the idempotency key only when intentionally creating another order.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/sandbox/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: local-synthetic-order-001
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Record ONE COMPLETE synthetic shipment; omitted items mean the entire Bag
# Shipment recording is local and does not buy a shipping label/contact a carrier.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/bags/{{bagId}}/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: local-shipment-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carrier": "USPS",
  "trackingNumber": "SANDBOX-TRACKING-0001",
  "trackingUrl": null
}

### Propose a FULL-BAG refund; this endpoint does not issue a payment refund
# An owner must review/approve the local proposal. Do not use partial amounts.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/bags/{{bagId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: local-refund-proposal-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Synthetic return requested for local testing"
}

### Read simulated payout/credit summary; requires payouts:read
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/payouts/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Read own catalog
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Queue a synthetic catalog import; requires catalog:write
# The tax code is intentionally a placeholder; it is NOT a tax classification.
# Catalog evidence/claims require human review before approval.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/products/import
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: local-catalog-import-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rows": [
    {
      "sku": "EXAMPLE-COTTON-01",
      "title": "Synthetic cotton product",
      "description": "Local catalog fixture; do not publish.",
      "category": "period-care/example",
      "priceCents": 2400,
      "inventoryQty": 10,
      "images": ["https://example.com/synthetic-product.png"],
      "variants": [],
      "evidence": {"ingredients_inci": ["Synthetic example material"], "certifications": [], "claims": [], "contraindications": ""},
      "taxCode": "REPLACE_WITH_REVIEWED_TAX_CODE",
      "shippingProfile": "standard"
    }
  ]
}

### Read import job progress after jobs run; requires catalog:read
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/products/import/{{importId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Set stock for an own SKU; requires catalog:write
# PATCH is not part of the POST idempotency store.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/inventory/EXAMPLE-COTTON-01
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"qty": 8}

### OPTIONAL: register an outbound webhook on an HTTPS endpoint YOU CONTROL
# This can cause REAL network requests by the worker. The .invalid placeholder
# is deliberately rejected; replace only when ready to receive sandbox events.
# The endpoint inherits allowed event families from this credential's scopes.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/webhook-endpoints
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: local-webhook-registration-001
Content-Type: application/json

{"url": "https://REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-ENDPOINT.invalid/avafem"}

### Replay an own event to an existing own endpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/webhook-endpoints/{{webhookEndpointId}}/replay
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: local-webhook-replay-001
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": "{{eventId}}"}

### OWNER: run the bounded worker now (local accounting/imports/handoffs;
# configured outbound endpoints may receive real HTTPS delivery attempts)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jobs/run
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### OWNER: create a private one-use onboarding invitation
# Open the returned /onboard/<token> path locally; do not share the token publicly.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/brands/{{brandId}}/invite
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### OWNER: Shopify preflight is a REAL READ-ONLY provider call if configured
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/connections/shopify/preflight
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### MCP initialize: use the same scoped Avafem bearer token
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
MCP-Protocol-Version: 2025-06-18
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"local-brand-example","version":"1.0.0"}}}

### MCP tool discovery
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
MCP-Protocol-Version: 2025-06-18
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/list","params":{}}

### MCP scoped Bag read
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
MCP-Protocol-Version: 2025-06-18
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"get_bag","arguments":{"id":"{{bagId}}"}}}

### MCP refund proposal ONLY; requires refunds:write and never issues money
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
MCP-Protocol-Version: 2025-06-18
Content-Type: application/json

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"refund_order","arguments":{"id":"{{bagId}}","refund":{"reason":"Synthetic MCP return proposal"},"idempotencyKey":"local-mcp-refund-001"}}}
